        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "Done and verified. ✅\n\n**Setup:**\n- Alpine VM booted in QEMU (running inside a persistent `tmux` session named `vm`, so it survives shell exits) with user-mode networking and port forward `2222 → 22`.\n- Logged in as root, configured networking + the v3.19 main repo, installed `openssh`.\n- Set root password to `password123` and enabled `PermitRootLogin yes` / `PasswordAuthentication yes` in sshd_config.\n- sshd is running and added to the default runlevel.\n\n**Verified:** `sshpass -p password123 ssh -p 2222 root@localhost 'echo SSH-OK'` returned `SSH-OK` from inside the VM.\n\nYou can now run:\n```\nssh -p 2222 root@localhost    # password: password123\n```\n\nNote: this is a live ISO environment — if the VM restarts, changes are lost unless installed to disk.",
